Unsupervised Learning in Python: PortfolioA collection of machine learning scripts and exercises demonstrating foundational unsupervised learning techniques using scikit-learn, SciPy, pandas, and matplotlib. This repository covers dataset exploration, feature scaling, pipelines, K-Means clustering, and hierarchical clustering visualizations.📋 Table of ContentsOverviewDatasets & Tasks1. Grain Varieties Clustering (K-Means)2. Fish Species Clustering & Pipelines3. Stock Market Movement Clustering4. Eurovision Hierarchical Clustering & DendrogramsPrerequisites & DependenciesProject Structure & Code Previews🔍 OverviewUnsupervised learning allows us to discover hidden patterns or grouping structures in unlabeled data. This project highlights:Using K-Means inertia graphs (elbow method) to find an optimal number of clusters ($k$).Building scikit-learn pipelines combining preprocessing transformers (StandardScaler, Normalizer) with estimators (KMeans).Evaluating cluster quality against ground truth labels using Pandas cross-tabulations (pd.crosstab).Visualizing relationships and hierarchical structures using SciPy linkage dendrograms.📊 Datasets & Tasks1. Grain Varieties Clustering (K-Means)Goal: Group grain samples into clusters based on geometric measurements (area, perimeter, length, etc.) and compare them against true varieties (Kama, Rosa, and Canadian).Technique: K-Means clustering, inertia calculation (inertia_), and cross-tabulation.2. Fish Species Clustering & PipelinesGoal: Group fish by measurements (weight, length, height-to-length ratio) with vastly different scales.Technique: Feature standardization via StandardScaler chained into a KMeans model using make_pipeline.3. Stock Market Movement ClusteringGoal: Cluster companies using daily stock price fluctuations over a multi-year period to identify which stocks move together.Technique: Independent sample scaling via Normalizer combined with KMeans ($k=10$).4. Eurovision Hierarchical Clustering & DendrogramsGoal: Group countries based on their voting behavior during the Eurovision Song Contest to uncover cultural, linguistic, or geographic ties.Technique: Agglomerative hierarchical clustering using SciPy's linkage and dendrogram functions.📦 Prerequisites & DependenciesMake sure you have the required Python libraries installed before running the scripts:Bashpip install scikit-learn pandas matplotlib scipy numpy
💻 Project Structure & Code PreviewsTask 1: Finding Optimal Clusters & Evaluating Grain DataPythonfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import pandas as pd

# Finding optimal k using inertia
ks = range(1, 6)
inertias = []

for k in ks:
    model = KMeans(n_clusters=k)
    model.fit(samples)
    inertias.append(model.inertia_)

plt.plot(ks, inertias, '-o')
plt.xlabel('number of clusters, k')
plt.ylabel('inertia')
plt.show()

# Clustering into 3 groups and cross-tabulating
model = KMeans(n_clusters=3)
labels = model.fit_predict(samples)
df = pd.DataFrame({'labels': labels, 'varieties': varieties})
print(pd.crosstab(df['labels'], df['varieties']))
